1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,271
A hotel stay usually has four main steps.

2
00:00:03,271 --> 00:00:07,361
First, you arrive and check in at the front desk.

3
00:00:07,361 --> 00:00:13,086
The staff confirms your reservation, checks your ID, and gives you a key card.

4
00:00:13,086 --> 00:00:17,584
Next, you ask any important questions before going to your room.

5
00:00:17,584 --> 00:00:24,537
Then, during your stay, you can ask for help with towels, Wi-Fi, cleaning, noise, or room problems.

6
00:00:24,537 --> 00:00:31,080
At the end, you check out, return the key card if needed, and check the bill.

7
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:34,351
Hotels do not all work the same way.

8
00:00:34,351 --> 00:00:39,668
A small hotel, a large chain hotel, and a resort can feel different.

9
00:00:39,668 --> 00:00:45,802
Still, the useful order is the same: confirm, ask, stay, solve problems, and check out.

10
00:00:45,802 --> 00:00:50,300
At check-in, hotel staff usually needs your reservation name and ID.

11
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:56,435
Depending on the hotel and country, this may be a passport or another photo ID.

12
00:00:56,435 --> 00:01:00,933
The staff may also ask for a card for extra costs.

13
00:01:00,933 --> 00:01:03,796
These extra costs are often called incidentals.

14
00:01:03,796 --> 00:01:08,703
They can include hotel food, minibar items, parking, damage, or other services.

15
00:01:08,703 --> 00:01:14,020
Sometimes the hotel only holds money on the card and releases it later.

16
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:18,927
The best check-in habit is to listen for numbers and repeat them.

17
00:01:18,927 --> 00:01:26,288
Room numbers, floors, breakfast times, Wi-Fi details, and check-out times are easy to misunderstand after a long trip.

18
00:01:26,288 --> 00:01:32,013
Before you leave the front desk, ask about the things that affect your stay.

19
00:01:32,013 --> 00:01:35,285
Ask whether breakfast is included or costs extra.

20
00:01:35,285 --> 00:01:39,375
Ask where breakfast is served and what time it starts.

21
00:01:39,375 --> 00:01:41,828
Ask how to connect to Wi-Fi.

22
00:01:41,828 --> 00:01:45,918
Ask where the elevator is if the hotel is large.

23
00:01:45,918 --> 00:01:53,688
If the room is not ready, ask when it will be ready and where you can leave your bags.

24
00:01:53,688 --> 00:01:58,186
This is not a phrase test. It is a planning moment.

25
00:01:58,186 --> 00:02:05,956
You are collecting the information you need so you do not have to come back downstairs tired and confused.

26
00:02:05,956 --> 00:02:09,228
During your stay, you may need small things.

27
00:02:09,228 --> 00:02:15,771
You may need extra towels, more toilet paper, a toothbrush, a blanket, or help with cleaning.

28
00:02:15,771 --> 00:02:21,497
In some hotels, housekeeping cleans every day. In other hotels, you need to ask.

29
00:02:21,497 --> 00:02:24,768
Some hotels put many items in the room.

30
00:02:24,768 --> 00:02:28,449
Other hotels keep extra items at the front desk.

31
00:02:28,449 --> 00:02:33,356
When you ask, start with your room number if you are calling.

32
00:02:33,356 --> 00:02:39,081
Then ask for one clear thing. If you need it soon, say that politely.

33
00:02:39,081 --> 00:02:43,989
The staff can help faster when your request is simple and specific.

34
00:02:43,989 --> 00:02:48,078
Room problems are normal. The air conditioner may not work.

35
00:02:48,078 --> 00:02:52,577
The room may be too cold. The Wi-Fi may be weak.

36
00:02:52,577 --> 00:02:55,030
A key card may stop working.

37
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:59,938
You may also have a small accident, such as breaking a glass.

38
00:02:59,938 --> 00:03:05,254
In these moments, do not hide the problem. Tell the front desk clearly.

39
00:03:05,254 --> 00:03:08,526
For safety problems, give the important facts first.

40
00:03:08,526 --> 00:03:13,024
Say your room number, what happened, and whether someone is hurt.

41
00:03:13,024 --> 00:03:16,705
If there is broken glass, do not touch it.

42
00:03:16,705 --> 00:03:24,884
If you feel unsafe because of noise or someone outside your room, call the front desk and ask for help.

43
00:03:24,884 --> 00:03:27,338
Checkout is the last hotel conversation.

44
00:03:27,338 --> 00:03:33,063
You may only need to say your room number and return the key card.

45
00:03:33,063 --> 00:03:35,926
But sometimes the bill has extra items.

46
00:03:35,926 --> 00:03:39,606
Look at the bill before you pay or leave.

47
00:03:39,606 --> 00:03:43,287
Check breakfast, parking, taxes, minibar items, or other fees.

48
00:03:43,287 --> 00:03:45,740
If something looks wrong, ask calmly.

49
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:50,239
At the end, ask for a receipt if you need one.

50
00:03:50,239 --> 00:03:57,600
If you need a taxi, a luggage room, or directions, checkout is also a good time to ask.

51
00:03:57,600 --> 00:04:01,281
A polite checkout conversation can finish the stay clearly.

52
00:04:01,281 --> 00:04:04,961
Practice these hotel situations after you understand the flow.

53
00:04:04,961 --> 00:04:07,006
Do not memorize every line.

54
00:04:07,006 --> 00:04:11,913
Use the situation, change one detail, and keep the key information clear.

55
00:04:11,913 --> 00:04:17,639
Receptionist: Good afternoon. Welcome to Riverside Hotel. How can I help you? Risa: Hi.

56
00:04:17,639 --> 00:04:21,319
I have a reservation under Ogino. Receptionist: Thank you.

57
00:04:21,319 --> 00:04:26,227
May I see your passport and card? Risa: Sure. Here you are.

58
00:04:26,227 --> 00:04:31,543
Receptionist: Thank you. You are staying for three nights. Risa: Yes, that's right.

59
00:04:31,543 --> 00:04:36,859
Receptionist: Your room is ready. You are in room 708. Risa: Room 708.

60
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:40,949
Thank you. Receptionist: We also need a card for incidentals.

61
00:04:40,949 --> 00:04:46,674
Risa: Is this a hold or a charge? Receptionist: It is only a hold.

62
00:04:46,674 --> 00:04:49,537
We release it after checkout. Risa: Okay.

63
00:04:49,537 --> 00:04:52,808
What kinds of extra costs does it cover?

64
00:04:52,808 --> 00:04:57,716
Receptionist: It can cover minibar items, parking, or damage. Risa: I understand.

65
00:04:57,716 --> 00:05:03,441
Thank you for explaining. Risa: Before I go upstairs, can I ask two questions?

66
00:05:03,441 --> 00:05:07,122
Receptionist: Of course. Risa: Is breakfast included? Receptionist: Yes.

67
00:05:07,122 --> 00:05:11,620
Breakfast is from 7 to 10 in the restaurant. Risa: Great.

68
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:14,074
How do I connect to Wi-Fi?

69
00:05:14,074 --> 00:05:19,799
Receptionist: The network and password are on your key card holder. Risa: Thank you.

70
00:05:19,799 --> 00:05:25,115
That helps. Receptionist: I am sorry, but your room is not ready yet.

71
00:05:25,115 --> 00:05:30,841
Risa: No problem. About what time will it be ready? Receptionist: Around 3 p.m.

72
00:05:30,841 --> 00:05:35,339
Risa: Can I leave my bags here until then? Receptionist: Yes.

73
00:05:35,339 --> 00:05:39,429
We can keep them behind the desk. Risa: Thank you.

74
00:05:39,429 --> 00:05:45,154
I will come back later. Front Desk: Front desk. How can I help you?

75
00:05:45,154 --> 00:05:50,470
Risa: Hi, this is room 708. Could I have two extra towels, please?

76
00:05:50,470 --> 00:05:55,787
Front Desk: Of course. Bath towels or hand towels? Risa: Bath towels, please.

77
00:05:55,787 --> 00:06:01,512
Front Desk: No problem. We will bring them shortly. Risa: Thank you very much.

78
00:06:01,512 --> 00:06:05,193
Front Desk: Front desk. How can I help you?

79
00:06:05,193 --> 00:06:10,100
Risa: Hi, this is room 708. The air conditioner is not working.

80
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:15,825
Front Desk: I am sorry about that. Is the room too warm? Risa: Yes.

81
00:06:15,825 --> 00:06:19,506
I tried the remote, but it does not change.

82
00:06:19,506 --> 00:06:24,413
Front Desk: I will send someone to check it. Risa: Thank you.

83
00:06:24,413 --> 00:06:30,139
How long will it take? Front Desk: About ten minutes. Front Desk: Front desk.

84
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:34,637
How can I help you? Risa: Hi, this is room 708.

85
00:06:34,637 --> 00:06:39,953
I accidentally broke a glass in the bathroom. Front Desk: Are you okay?

86
00:06:39,953 --> 00:06:43,634
Did you get hurt? Risa: No, I am okay.

87
00:06:43,634 --> 00:06:46,906
But there is broken glass on the floor.

88
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:51,813
Front Desk: Please do not touch it. We will send housekeeping now.

89
00:06:51,813 --> 00:06:57,538
Risa: Thank you. I am sorry about that. Front Desk: No problem. Accidents happen.

90
00:06:57,538 --> 00:07:01,219
Front Desk: Front desk. How can I help you?

91
00:07:01,219 --> 00:07:06,535
Risa: Hi, this is room 708. There is loud noise near my room.

92
00:07:06,535 --> 00:07:12,261
Front Desk: I am sorry. Is it coming from the hallway or another room?

93
00:07:12,261 --> 00:07:15,941
Risa: I think it is from the next room.

94
00:07:15,941 --> 00:07:20,440
Front Desk: Thank you for telling us. We will check it.

95
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:24,529
Risa: If it continues, is it possible to change rooms?

96
00:07:24,529 --> 00:07:29,845
Front Desk: We will try to help if the noise does not stop.

97
00:07:29,845 --> 00:07:34,753
Receptionist: Good morning. Are you checking out? Risa: Yes. Room 708, please.

98
00:07:34,753 --> 00:07:40,069
Receptionist: Thank you. Here is your bill. Risa: Could I check one charge?

99
00:07:40,069 --> 00:07:44,977
Receptionist: Of course. Which one? Risa: What is this minibar charge for?

100
00:07:44,977 --> 00:07:49,475
Receptionist: Let me check. I am sorry, that was a mistake.

101
00:07:49,475 --> 00:07:54,791
I will remove it. Risa: Thank you. Could I have a receipt, please?
